# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PaperPrototyping toolbox
#
# The predecessor repo (PaperVoxels) grew to 652 MB because exported artefacts,
# zipped snapshots and texture libraries were committed as if they were source.
# Everything below is the stuff that caused that. Keep it out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Exported artefacts -----------------------------------------------------
# Every tool writes timestamped PDF/SVG here. These are outputs, not source.
output/
**/output/

# --- Version snapshots ------------------------------------------------------
# Use a git branch or tag instead of a dated copy of the folder.
*.zip
*_backup/
*_old/
* - Copy/
*_v[0-9]*_[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/

# --- User art assets --------------------------------------------------------
# Panel/lid/strip artwork is personal media, often 8 MB+ per .tif. The tools
# generate placeholder assets at startup, so the sketches run without these.
# See PaperPolyhedra/data/README.md.
**/data/*.tif
**/data/*.tiff
**/data/*.psd
**/data/*.jpg
**/data/*.jpeg
**/data/*.png
**/data/*.webp
**/data/*.pdf
**/data/panels/
**/data/lids/

# Re-include the small files the sketches genuinely need to run.
!**/data/*.txt
!**/data/*.json
!**/data/README.md
!**/data/.gitkeep

# --- Processing -------------------------------------------------------------
applet/
application.linux*/
application.windows*/
application.macosx*/
*.class

# --- OS / editor cruft ------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
._*
__MACOSX/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*.tmp
*.bak
*~

# --- Local tooling ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
